      ":question/problem": "$f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid - 2) = {\\frac{4}{x^{5}},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables.\nFind the conditional variance $Var\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid - 2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $\u03bc_{X \\mid - 2} = \\frac{4}{3}$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
